From 705a61ccd9dbfc28d76d016180b56fa867cb97ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: fmillion <47171880+fmillion@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 08:31:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 28/42] Bluetooth: hci_intel: set the serdev drvdata in
 intel_serdev_probe()

hci_serdev.c finds the hci_uart through the serdev drvdata. Without it
all received data is dropped (WARN in hci_uart_receive_buf() /
hci_uart_write_wakeup()) and setup fails with "Reading Intel version
information failed (-110)".

Found by the Samsung Galaxy Book S (Lakefield) work,
github.com/franke7777/galaxy-book-s-linux (dkms/books-bt).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/bluetooth/hci_intel.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_intel.c b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_intel.c
index 44a970e63..e85490cb8 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_intel.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_intel.c
@@ -1320,6 +1320,8 @@ static int intel_serdev_probe(struct serdev_device *serdev)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
 	hu->serdev = serdev;
+	/* hci_serdev.c looks the hci_uart up through the drvdata */
+	serdev_device_set_drvdata(serdev, hu);
 
 	/* The port is not open yet (hci_uart_register_device() opens it), so
 	 * only the ACPI properties and the reset GPIO can be used here.
-- 
